        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "The transpose $\\mathbf{A}^{\\top}$ of a matrix $\\mathbf{A}=[a_{jk}]$ is $\\mathbf{A}^{\\top}=[a_{jk}]$; rows become columns and conversely (Sec. 7.2). Here, $\\mathbf{A}$ need not be square. If it is and $\\mathbf{A}=\\mathbf{A}^{\\top}$, then $\\mathbf{A}$ is called symmetric; if $\\mathbf{A}=-\\mathbf{A}^{\\top}$, it is called skew-symmetric.\nFor a product, $(\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{B})^{\\top}=\\mathbf{B}^{\\top}\\mathbf{A}^{\\top}$ (Sec. 7.2).",
